  "flock.review.title": "Review queue",
  "flock.rules.believe.basics": "Parrots also need 10 to 12 hours of quiet, dark sleep, clean air (no nonstick cookware, aerosols, or scented candles near them), and daily social time with their people.",
  "flock.rules.believe.bridge": "The Flock brings researchers, conservationists, and parrot owners together. Our care recommendations come from avian research and veterinary science, and our mission is a place where all of us collaborate.",
  "flock.rules.believe.bridgeLead": "We're bridging research and life with birds.",
  "flock.rules.believe.diet": "We advocate for a varied, fresh diet built on fresh foods and a quality pellet.",
  "flock.rules.believe.flight": "Research shows how beneficial flight is for birds, so we advocate for keeping them fully flighted whenever possible.",
  "flock.rules.believe.husbandry": "We advocate for good husbandry, which means an appropriately sized cage, daily enrichment, plenty of foraging, and time out of the cage.",
  "flock.rules.believe.intro": "The Flock is a place to get better at caring for parrots, together. These beliefs shape everything else on this page.",
  "flock.rules.believe.standardsLead": "A few things are non-negotiable for us, because the research is clear.",
  "flock.rules.believe.table": "We separate the issue from the person. Most of us didn't know all of this when we started, and all of us are still learning. Parrots aren't domesticated the way dogs and cats are, so we're figuring out how to do better together. Wherever you and your bird are today, you're welcome here, and if you're committed to doing better, we want you in the Flock.",
  "flock.rules.believe.tableLead": "Most importantly, we're building a bigger table.",
  "flock.rules.believe.title": "What we believe",
  "flock.rules.believe.training": "We train with positive reinforcement, because research shows it's the best way to train and bond with a bird. We don't advocate for dominance or punishment-based methods.",
  "flock.rules.believe.vet": "We never give medical advice here. You're welcome to share what's worked for you, but none of us are avian vets, and posts that give medical advice will be taken down.",
  "flock.rules.believe.vetLead": "Health questions go to an avian vet.",
  "flock.rules.believe.wild": "That's why part of every membership goes to rescue and conservation partners, and why we choose those partners together.",
  "flock.rules.believe.wildLead": "Caring for the bird at home is connected to protecting parrots in the wild.",
  "flock.rules.rules.age": "Members must be 18 or older.",
  "flock.rules.rules.broken": "Most of the time, it starts with a private note from the Kya team. If it keeps happening, the content comes down, then the member's account is paused for 30 days, and after that they're removed from the Flock. Harassment, hateful content, animal cruelty, sharing someone's personal information, and selling birds lead straight to removal. Anyone removed from the Flock gets a refund for the unused part of their membership.",
  "flock.rules.rules.brokenLead": "What happens when a rule is broken.",
  "flock.rules.rules.clipping": "No how-to content for wing clipping, and no posts encouraging others to clip. Sharing your own bird's history is fine.",
  "flock.rules.rules.harassment": "No harassment, bullying, threats, or hateful content toward anyone, for any reason.",
  "flock.rules.rules.harm": "No content showing or encouraging harm to an animal, including punishment-based training like hitting, yelling, spraying, \"dominance\" techniques, or withholding food to force a behavior.",
  "flock.rules.rules.intro": "These are the firm lines. We have zero tolerance for harassment, hateful content, or anything that harms people or animals.",
  "flock.rules.rules.medical": "No diagnosing another member's bird or recommending medications or doses. Share your own experience, and if something sounds urgent, tell them to call an avian vet now.",
  "flock.rules.rules.objectionable": "No sexual, graphic, or otherwise objectionable content.",
  "flock.rules.rules.personal": "No sharing anyone's personal information, including addresses, phone numbers, and private messages.",
  "flock.rules.rules.selling": "No selling, trading, or breeding birds, and no posts asking where to buy one. If you need to rehome a bird, the Kya team will point you to a partner rescue.",
  "flock.rules.rules.spam": "No spam, affiliate links, or business promotion. You can recommend products you love, and fundraising belongs in Do good, where it's reviewed first.",
  "flock.rules.rules.title": "The rules",
  "flock.rules.treat.experience": "Share your own experience. \"Here's what helped when we switched off seeds\" teaches more than \"you're doing it wrong.\" Talk about what worked for you rather than telling someone what they have to do.",
  "flock.rules.treat.feedback": "Give feedback when it's asked for. If someone posts \"What do you think of my setup?\", thoughtful, constructive feedback is welcome. If someone just shares a photo of their bird, celebrate the bird. If something in it worries you, flag it and let the Kya team follow up privately.",
  "flock.rules.treat.intent": "Assume good intent. Nearly everyone here is trying to do right by their bird, including the people who are newest to this.",
  "flock.rules.treat.intro": "This is the heart of the Flock. It's what makes this place different from the groups many of us left.",
  "flock.rules.treat.kind": "Be kind in the comments. Talk to people the way you'd want someone to talk to you on a hard day with your bird.",
  "flock.rules.treat.pileOn": "Never pile on. If you see someone getting a lot of critique, don't add to it. Flag it if it's gone too far.",
  "flock.rules.treat.privacy": "Respect privacy. Don't share someone else's personal details, location, or messages, and don't screenshot posts to share outside the Flock.",
  "flock.rules.treat.title": "How we treat each other",
  "flock.rules.works.chapter": "Your chapter is your local corner of the Flock. If a bird is lost or found near you, post it there right away. Please share the general area only, never your home address or your bird's leg band or microchip number.",
  "flock.rules.works.contact": "Questions or concerns about the community can always go to the Kya team at {{email}}.",
  "flock.rules.works.flagging": "Flagging is how we keep the Flock kind. If something looks harmful, unkind, or out of line with the care standards above, flag it and add a note if you'd like. You don't need to correct anyone yourself.",
  "flock.rules.works.journeys": "Journeys are where members share the skills they're teaching their birds, along with what's working and what isn't.",
  "flock.rules.works.private": "What you share stays in the Flock. We'll never feature your posts, photos, or videos anywhere else without asking you first.",
  "flock.rules.works.review": "The Kya team reviews every flag. Harmful content is handled within 24 hours. When a post goes against our care standards, someone from the Kya team reaches out to that member privately, never with a public correction.",
  "flock.rules.works.spaces": "Start here is for introductions and getting your bearings. Learn together is for questions, setups, and what you're working on. Do good is for rescue and conservation needs, and posts there are reviewed before they go live.",
  "flock.rules.works.title": "How the Flock works",
  "flock.setup.birds": "Which birds should members meet?",
